From cd64f601bd7df196ddd777933dc3d9bf52919966 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 06:36:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Solvers of Trilinos on the host, third review

Tpetra computes where MFEM computes: the solvers are implemented by a
class template over the node of Tpetra (TrilinosTpetraBackend.hxx),
instantiated for the default node, on the GPU when Trilinos is built for
one, and for the serial node (or the OpenMP node) of the host, used when
MFEM computes on the host. Before, Trilinos built with CUDA always
computed on the GPU. FROSch keeps the default node: FROSch 17.2.1 runs
some loops in the default execution space of Kokkos whatever the node.
A Krylov solver of Belos computes on the node of its preconditioner of
Trilinos.

Third review:
- the hybrid GMRES is the only solver reset when the matrix changes
  (GCRODR and the native solvers of Tpetra throw on a reset before the
  vectors are given);
- the settings of mfem-mgis (tolerance, maximum number of iterations,
  verbosity, restarts of GMRES) are given to the backend apart from the
  parameters of Belos, and added only when the solver accepts them; the
  hybrid GMRES and its aliases are detected by the parameters they
  accept, its outer solver is checked with the generic factory of Belos,
  and its default tolerance is the one of the outer solver; LSQR and the
  native solvers of Tpetra, which ignore the unknown parameters, are not
  checked;
- the block relaxations of Ifpack2 are not checked without matrix (they
  read the matrix when their parameters are set);
- MueLu: the default parameters of mfem-mgis are only set in the
  simplified syntax;
- CMake: the configuration files of Kokkos are compared (views of
  Spack);
- tests: GCRODR, native GMRES of Tpetra, GMRESPOLY, block relaxation,
  hybrid GMRES on a second system of another size, refusals of LSQR with
  a tolerance and of a native outer solver.
